---
// Accessibility notes shared by every chart page.
interface Props {
  /** What the arrow keys move between, for example "categories" or "slices". */
  items?: string;
}

const { items = 'categories' } = Astro.props;
---

<ul>
  <li>Give every chart a <code>label</code>. It names the chart for screen readers and captions its data table.</li>
  <li>
    The plot is focusable. The arrow keys move between {items}, Home and End jump to the ends, Escape clears the
    focus and Enter selects. Each move is announced with its values.
  </li>
  <li>A visually hidden table carries the same data, so screen reader users can read every value in order.</li>
  <li>Legend entries are buttons that report whether their series is shown.</li>
  <li>Animations are skipped when the user prefers reduced motion, or always with <code>disable-animation</code>.</li>
  <li>
    Colors come from the <a href='/charts/theming/'>chart palette</a>. Do not rely on color alone: keep the legend,
    or add value labels.
  </li>
</ul>
